{"e":{"No-Go":[{"p":"noun","g":"n","i":"/ˈnɔʊ̯ɡɔʊ̯/","a":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/d/d9/De-No-Go.ogg/De-No-Go.ogg.mp3","s":[["no go (something which should not or cannot be done)",["colloquial"],[]]],"fm":[["No-Gos","genitive"],["No-Gos","plural"],["No-Go","nominative singular"],["No-Gos","definite nominative plural"],["No-Gos","genitive singular"],["No-Gos","definite genitive plural"],["No-Go","dative singular"],["No-Gos","dative definite plural"],["No-Go","accusative singular"],["No-Gos","accusative definite plural"]],"et":"Borrowed from English no go.","r":6}]},"f":{"no-gos":[["No-Go","genitive"],["No-Go","plural"],["No-Go","definite nominative plural"],["No-Go","genitive singular"],["No-Go","definite genitive plural"],["No-Go","dative definite plural"],["No-Go","accusative definite plural"],["No-Go","accusative dative genitive nominative plural"]]},"x":{"No-Go":{"l":["Aktuell schon keine allzu angenehme Ecke wird es dann wahrscheinlich zur No-Go Area.","Ein spezielles Restaurant sei für den einen ein No-Go, für den anderen das Lieblingsrestaurant.","Er bezeichnet die Aktion, bei der Vizekanzler Robert Habeck seine Fähre nicht verlassen konnte, als \"No-Go\"."]}}}